Empty mileage: 18% of kilometers traveled without cargo. The goal is 14% in six months. One percentage point is roughly 2.1 million rubles per year.

Where empty mileage comes from, based on last quarter's data:
— 61%—the trip was originally planned one-way, and no return load was sought;
— 22%—a return order existed but appeared in the system after the truck departed;
— 11%—positioning a truck to a client in another city;
— 6%—other.

Drivers sometimes take side cargo themselves, bypassing the system: 40 trips went this way last quarter, with cash paid directly to the driver.
